From 04ae5ec8461a0c8989c3ce6173770c447291c28f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A9 project <dmayala@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:27:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/a9_eink: fixed-mode CRTC enabled from reset; any
 framebuffer size

Mainline Android run 6: every drm_hwcomposer commit to the a9_eink card
failed in the DRM core ("[CRTC] active without enabled", -EINVAL): the
composer believes the one mode is already set and commits ACTIVE=1 + FB
with no MODE_ID and no connector link. Small layer imports also failed
("bad framebuffer height 49": mode_config min = max = 824x1648).

- The CRTC is ENABLED with the fixed 824x1648 mode from reset on (active
  false) and its connector is routed to it after drm_mode_config_reset; a
  commit that would disable it (MODE_ID 0, connector CRTC_ID 0) is turned
  into "inactive, mode and link kept" in the driver's mode_config check, so
  a later ACTIVE-only commit passes the core check.
- The CRTC's own check requires the primary plane only while active.
- mode_config 1x1 .. 4096x4096; the primary plane's check (no scaling, no
  positioning) still requires a full 824x1648 source on the only plane.

Power/drive path unchanged: enabled/active of this virtual card powers
nothing. HV comes up only when the worker runs an update (pixels changed
against the shadow, a9_eink.enable, both power gates), with the same caps,
interlock, template and bin window; an active CRTC without a changed
framebuffer kicks no update.
KUnit (CONFIG_DRM_A9_EINK_KUNIT_TEST, a9_eink_kms_test.c, #included so it
runs the driver's own a9_kms_init and checks; .kunitconfig): initial state
enabled/inactive with the fixed mode and connector routed; an ACTIVE-only
commit (ACTIVE=1 + plane FB, no MODE_ID, no connector) passes
drm_atomic_check_only; a committed full disable keeps mode and link and an
ACTIVE-only check passes after it; an 824x49 fb is creatable but refused on
the plane. 4/4 pass on arm64 QEMU; with the stock CRTC reset the first two
fail. KMS init factored into a9_kms_init() (probe order unchanged).
Review 12 (NO-GO) fixes:
- the reset state's connector link takes the connector reference a linked
  connector state owns (released by the helper's destroy); the disable
  rewrite links through drm_atomic_set_crtc_for_connector (which does);
- the seeded mode is prepared like a userspace MODE_ID
  (drm_mode_set_crtcinfo: crtc_clock/htotal/vtotal) and adjusted_mode is set,
  so the virtual vblank timer runs after an ACTIVE-only commit from reset;
- a connector-only detach (connector CRTC_ID 0) is normalized too: the CRTC
  state is taken with the normal error/backoff conventions, the link
  restored, the CRTC forced inactive;
- on driver removal (kms_teardown) a disable really unlinks, so the
  connector is released before drm_mode_config_cleanup.
KUnit now commits from reset: ACTIVE+FB, ACTIVE=0, ACTIVE+FB, MODE_ID=0,
ACTIVE+FB, connector-only CRTC_ID=0, ACTIVE+FB; after each: enabled, fixed
mode with derived timings, adjusted_mode, connector routed; after each
ACTIVE: framedur 16-17.5 ms and flip_done well under the 10 s timeout; the
connector refcount at reset = 2; the run fails on any kernel WARN (leak,
refcount, vblank). Mutations (no connector get, no crtcinfo, stock reset)
are caught.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
